There is not enough information to verify the claim because the record lacks evidence regarding Twitter's moderation actions or whether they placed warnings on tweets containing the clips of Joe Biden. While a [USA Today fact-check](https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/06/19/fact-check-joe-biden-doesnt-want-ban-all-fracking-only-new-permits/3215253001/) confirms that during a July 2019 debate Biden stated he would make sure fracking is "eliminated," his official campaign policy as of October 2020 was to only ban new fracking projects on public lands and waters, as reported by [Newsweek](https://www.newsweek.com/video-resurfaces-kamala-harris-saying-she-wants-ban-fracking-after-saying-biden-will-not-during-1537304). Without documentation of Twitter's actions or warning labels on these specific tweets, a final determination cannot be made.